    "summary": "- Tokens are generated as `tly_` plus 40 random `[A-Za-z0-9]` characters via crypto/rand. Only the SHA-256 hex hash and last4 are stored. The full token appears only in the create and invite-accept responses.\n- Auth hashes the presented token. Old plain-text snapshot tokens still load and authenticate, and the next snapshot contains no plain-text token. `last_used_at` is written at most once a minute per key.\n- `go build ./...`, `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` pass, with new tests covering the hashing, the leak paths, legacy migration and the throttle.",
